MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Also, it's really really really hard to write functions like kfold that handle all possible things a user can do when specifying a model. This is the curse of R's flexibility. It's nice to be able to write the same model in many ways but that also means it's a nightmare to make sure all of those specifications are compatible with every thing you might want to do after the fact. It would be much easier if we allowed fewer ways of specifying the same model.

