Hi Daniel,

I haven't done any pre-processing, although your question made me realise that in these runs I didn't standardise the data before fitting it (I did in earlier runs though, and the issue was there too).
I'm calling Stan via Python (PyStan), so I would expect the printed lists to be 0-indexed.
The NaN Rhats haven't been bothering me so far — for example, if a = 'alpha[3]' is the cubic coefficient, but the trend is quadratic, I figured there would be uncertainty in a near zero, and the chains would have trouble converging there.
Kevin

