Yes, that can help.

And also, vectorizing this

>>> for(t in 2:N)
>>>   y[t] ~ normal(y[t-1], sigma_dynamic);
>>> }

as

y[2:N] ~ normal(y[1:(N - 1)], sigma_dynamic);

will speed the iterations up.

- Bob

