Oh, one thing I forgot to mention is the behaviour of models with simpler location polynomials (C < 4) — they seem to sample quickly again. This was one of the things that confused me originally: it seemed like the trouble only arose when the scale's polynomial was less expressive than the location's. So using two quadratic polynomials is fine, and using two degree-4 polynomials is fine too, but there's a difficulty in exploring the posterior (which I wouldn't have predicted) that arises when using one degree-2 polynomial and one degree-4 polynomial.

