Problem solved <https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=footer#!msg/shinyapps-users/hzmzb_jnoAA/_6lrr9y1BgAJ>: the commit from which `devtools::install_github` pulls (when installing the R package I've built, named RescueTimeEstimator) pertains to the most recent commit that is installed on the machine from which you deploy to Shinyapps. In my case, that was the initial commit (so, while I made plenty of incremental changes and pushed them diligently to GitHub/master, none of them were being sent to the shinyapps server).

Finally, for information, the `RescueTimeEstimator.so` and `Modules.o` files should not be included on GitHub. (These are the files that are generated when the Stan code is compiled into C++ code, but before the encompassing R package itself is built).

Thanks so much for your time, feedback and pull request. Happy Monday!

