Is it currently possible to specify a correlation matrix with common restrictions on the support for all matrix entries (or at least the non-diagonals)? Such that the below could be specified and compile successfully:

corr_matrix<lower=0,upper=1>[D] restrictedMatrix;

An equivalent solution would be a general matrix[D,D] with diagonals = 1, non-diagonals restricted between 0 and 1 and with symmetry enforced, but I've been unable to specify such a matrix.

A related question is whether setting this type of restriction on a correlation matrix is even a good idea in the first place from a sampling perspective, is it liable to result in poor HMC behaviour?

