> The model (below) is similar to the PPCA model in the ADVI paper. So some of the reasons why ADVI worked well for those models sort of applies here. Stan fits it with NUTS pretty quickly actually. The problem is that N_eff is low for some of the variables, like 3 for mu_F and 10 for lp__

When you get an estimated N_eff of 3, that means either the convergence of chains did not occur or they did not even move appreciably. But neither of those will happen if the posterior distribution is even roughly multivariate normal, which is what full-rank ADVI is using to approximate the posterior. In the meanfield case, the approximation is multivariate normal but with dimensions that are independent.

