If this is a problem for the model I posted above, then it is also a problem for the PPCA/ARD model in Figure 23 in the ADVI paper. I just ran NUTS on that exact model with my simulated data. With M=1, I got 2 / 1000 effective samples for the alpha and lp__ parameters (rhats around 10). With M=2, I got 2 / 1000 for both alphas (and rhats > 10), but a reasonable number for lp__.

