MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Because

  uniform(y | a, b) = 1 / (b - a)

so

  log uniform(y | a, b) = -log(b - a)

so

  log uniform(y | 0, T) = -log(T)

Doesn't matter how small (b - a) is.

- Bob

