Subject: Re: [stan-users] matrix notation error
Message-ID: <tU8CIaWsumc.Zv-tgY0cDwAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <tU8CIaWsumc.RPV5fOARDwAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
References: <tU8CIaWsumc.RPV5fOARDwAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/tU8CIaWsumc/m/Zv-tgY0cDwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The model in section 8.13 (pg 145 & 146) demonstrates how to take in a matrix of predictors as I believe you want. You need to declare X to be a Nx2 matrix in the data block, beta as a Nx2 matrix in the parameters block, nix the creation of mu, and simply do:

    y ~ normal( rows_dot_product( x , beta[subj] ) , sigma) ;

in the parameters block.

