Thanks! Well, you start with 5 parameters in the original formulation, but the actual family we consider has only 2 (briefly, you lose one parameter because you restrict the two normals to have equal variances so that p(Y|X) is monotonic in X; then you lose another two because you can show that all that matters for the distribution of p(Y|X) is the difference in the means divided by the standard deviation. In the end the distribution is parameterized by the probability of being in the positive class and the separation between the two classes).

