I should have noted that I got around 500 effective samples for the 45 minutes of runtime (timing is for 4 chains in parallel), which is only about 0.18 effective samples per second. If you need more effective samples you'll need to run the sampler for longer. You'll likely get lower effective samples per second on real data.

Rob

On Tue, Feb 28, 2017 at 2:11 PM, Nick Menzies <nick.m...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Great, thanks for the quick feedback (Rob, Aki, Bob, Andrew)!
>
> I will give this a go and report back. 45 minutes is certainly reasonable so if I can get somewhere close to that it will be great.
>
